    {
        "content": "<p>jrandolf edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14843\">PR #14843</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This adds map support where Wasmtime prints and parses WAVE values, using wasm-tools 1.263.0, now on <code>main</code> via #15097:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>wasmtime run --invoke</code>, <code>Val::to_wave</code> and <code>Val::from_wave</code> print and parse maps as <code>{key: value, ...}</code> (<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasm-tools/issues/2782\">bytecodealliance/wasm-tools#2782</a>). WAVE merges duplicate keys, keeping the last value.</li>\n<li><code>map-types.wast</code> uses the existing <code>map.const</code> support to check that guest-returned maps and map arguments retain duplicate keys. This covers the duplicate-keys test that #14834 dropped, as suggested there.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">model</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">echo</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Closes #14811<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637017679,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793653521
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>jrandolf edited <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14843\">PR #14843</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Component maps are currently unsupported by Wasmtime's WAVE integration. Implement the wasm-wave map traits for <code>component::Type</code> and <code>component::Val</code> in <code>crates/wasmtime/src/runtime/wave/component.rs</code>, enabling <code>Val::to_wave</code>, <code>Val::from_wave</code>, and <code>wasmtime run --invoke</code> to handle maps through the existing parsing and display helpers.</p>\n<p>WAVE merges duplicate keys, keeping the last value:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"cp\">$</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">W</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">model</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">invoke</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"na\">echo</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">4</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">})</span><span class=\"o\">'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tests</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">all</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">cli_tests</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">component</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">map</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">wat</span>\n<span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>CLI tests cover empty maps, map arguments and results, and duplicate keys. WAST tests use the existing <code>map.const</code> support to check that <code>Val::Map</code> retains duplicate entries when lowering arguments and lifting results.</p>\n<p>Closes #14811<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637019564,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793654049
    },
